Objective

Identify a SQL injection vulnerability in the product category filter and retrieve the database version using a UNION-based SQL Injection attack.

Skills Practiced
SQL Injection Detection
UNION-Based SQL Injection
Burp Suite Repeater
Identifying Number of Columns
Finding Text-Compatible Columns
Retrieving Database Version
Methodology
Step 1

Intercepted the request using Burp Suite Repeater.

Step 2

Confirmed SQL injection by modifying the vulnerable parameter.

Step 3

Determined the number of columns returned by the query.

Step 4

Identified which columns accepted text values.

Step 5

Retrieved the database version using a UNION SELECT query.

Concepts Learned
UNION SQL Injection
SQL Comment Syntax
Database Version Enumeration
Text-Compatible Columns
Manual Web Application Testing
Tools Used
Burp Suite Community Edition
PortSwigger Web Security Academy
Google Chrome
Outcome
Successfully identified the SQL injection vulnerability.
Retrieved the database version.
Understood the process of UNION-based SQL Injection.
